
SALT TRANSCRIPT-GENERATION SETTINGS MANIFEST — HARDER, WIDER-SPECTRUM DESIGN
====================================================================================

TOTAL: 180 transcripts
- 150 single-convention transcripts: 10 conventions × 3 difficulties × 5 transcripts
- 30 final mixed-convention transcripts: 10 Easy + 10 Medium + 10 Hard

GLOBAL DESIGN PRINCIPLES
- Generate every transcript in a separate independent model call.
- Keep the generation model, reasoning setting, master prompt, age range, speaker ratio, and output format fixed.
- Difficulty differs sharply in transcript length, candidate density, edge-case proportion, syntactic complexity, and SALT-feature complexity.
- All conventions at the same difficulty use identical quantitative settings.
- Edge cases are a subset of the controlled target-plus-distractor candidate occurrences, not additional cases.
- Avoid lexical repetition and repeated sentence patterns so performance cannot be inflated by local pattern continuation.

SINGLE-CONVENTION DESIGN
Easy: 32 utterances; 12 targets; 10 distractors; 9 edge cases (~41%)
Medium: 52 utterances; 20 targets; 20 distractors; 24 edge cases (60%)
Hard: 76 utterances; 30 targets; 34 distractors; 45 edge cases (~70%)

